# Gatsby files
.cache/
# NOTE: upstream's boilerplate ignored `public` here, which is right for Gatsby
# (where it's build output) and wrong for Vite (where it's committed source that
# gets copied into dist/ verbatim). It was silently keeping public/404.html — the
# file that makes deep links work on GitHub Pages — out of the repo.

